AEMS — Autonomous Energy Monitoring System
Licensing
==========================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Vignesh Selvaraj, Aditya Nagaraj, Shengyuan Zhang,
Sina Sadeghian, and Sangkee Min
Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of Wisconsin–Madison.

AEMS is a mixed hardware + software + documentation project. Because these are
legally different kinds of work, different parts of this repository are released
under different licenses, as follows.

  * Hardware design files  ->  CERN-OHL-P-2.0   (permissive open hardware)
      Applies to: hardware/ (KiCad schematics and PCB, custom libraries, BOM,
      manufacturing/fabrication outputs, and other hardware design source).
      Full text: LICENSES/CERN-OHL-P-2.0.txt   (see also hardware/LICENSE)

  * Firmware and host software  ->  MIT
      Applies to: the original source code in firmware/ and the Python
      BoardInterfaceLibrary authored by the AEMS project (excluding vendor and
      third-party components listed below).
      Full text: LICENSES/MIT.txt   (see also firmware/LICENSE)

  * Documentation and figures  ->  CC-BY-4.0
      Applies to: README files, the docs/ directories, design summaries, and
      other written documentation and figures authored by the AEMS project.
      Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

SPDX license expression for the repository as a whole:

    CERN-OHL-P-2.0 AND MIT AND CC-BY-4.0

Full, unmodified copies of each license are stored in the LICENSES/ directory,
named by SPDX identifier (following the REUSE specification, https://reuse.software).


Third-party components
----------------------

Vendor and third-party components are NOT covered by the licenses above and
retain their own licenses, including but not limited to:

  * STMicroelectronics STM32H7xx HAL / CMSIS / BSP drivers
      (firmware/Drivers/ — see the LICENSE.txt files there)
  * FreeRTOS  (firmware/Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/)
  * OpenAMP / libmetal
  * FatFs
  * BlueNRG-2  (firmware/Middlewares/ST/BlueNRG-2/)
  * Third-party KiCad symbol/footprint libraries under
    hardware/CustomLibs/Downloaded/

Nothing in this file overrides or modifies the terms of any third-party
component. Where a file carries its own license or copyright notice, that notice
governs that file.


Attribution / how to cite
--------------------------

If you use AEMS in academic work, please cite the accompanying paper and, where
appropriate, this repository. See CITATION.cff and the README.

Contact: Vignesh Selvaraj <vselvaraj@wisc.edu> or <vignesh-selvaraj@outlook.com>
